.\" -*- coding: utf-8; tab-width: 4; indent-tabs-mode: t; -*- vim: noet ts=4
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt DSCLEAN 1
.Os macOS
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm dsclean
.Nd recursively purge a directory of .DS_Store files
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl gpq
.Op Pa directory
.Nm
.Op Fl gpq
.Fl h
.Nm
.Fl t
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
recursively cleans
.Ar directory
of .DS_Store files generated by macOS's Finder,
preserving directory modification times if possible.
If
.Ar directory
is omitted,
the current working directory is used instead.
.
.\" Options
.ad l
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Fl g
Exclude .DS_Store files that are tracked by a Git repository.
This can prevent accidental modification of a project or one of its submodules.
.Pp
Note that Git is required to use this option;
if the
.Fl g
switch is passed, but the
.Xr git 1
executable could not be found in the user's
.Ev PATH ,
.Nm
terminates with an error code before proceeding with its search.
.
.It Fl p
Include partially-matching filenames such as
.Pa Junk.DS_Store .
Only suffixes are matched;
a filename of
.Pa .DS_Store.Junk
will not be affected by this option.
.
.It Fl t , -test
Run built-in unit tests.
Requires
.Xr shellcheck 1 ,
.Xr mandoc 1 ,
and a writable
.Pa /tmp
directory.
.El
.
.Ss Deprecated options
These options are retained for backwards compatibility only,
and their use is discouraged in favour of shell redirection.
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Fl h , -home
Target the user's home directory,
discarding any error messages emitted by
.Xr find 1
during the search
.Pq because certain directories are private on macOS .
Analogous to
.Ql Nm No ~ Pf 2> Pa /dev/null .
.
.It Fl q
Suppress all output.
Analogous to
.Ql Nm Pf > Pa /dev/null .
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.ad l
.de NC
.	ie n .Em no-color.org
.	el   .Lk no-color.org
..
.Bl -tag -width FORCE_COLOUR
.It Ev FORCE_COLOR
If set to a non-empty string,
terminal highlighting will be used unconditionally,
even when output is redirected.
This variable takes precedence over
.Ev NO_COLOR ,
and its exact value is immaterial.
Note that
.Nm Ap s
support for the
.Ev FORCE_COLOR
variable is an unofficial extension to the
.NC
specification.
.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty string,
terminal highlighting (colours and bold text) are suppressed,
even when output is attached to a TTY.
Consult
.NC
for details of the specification honoured by
.Nm .
.El
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -ohang
.It Sy "Required commands not found"
One or more executables required for
.Nm
to function was not found in the user's
.Ev PATH .
These include
.Xr basename 1 ,
.Xr dirname 1 ,
.Xr format-bytes 1 ,
and
.Xr utime 1 .
.It Sy "conflicting options given: -h and -t"
.Nm
was invoked with both
.Fl -run-tests
and the
.Fl -home
options enabled,
requesting two fundamentally incompatible modes of operation.
.It Sy "Git is required to use the -g option; aborting"
The
.Fl g
switch was passed,
but
.Xr git 1
could not be found in the user's
.Ev PATH .
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chflags 1 ,
.Xr find 1 ,
.Xr format-bytes 1 ,
.Xr rm 1 ,
.Xr Mac::Finder::DSStore 3 ,
.Xr dot_clean 8
.
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was first written on March 22nd 2015 \
as its author's first attempt at shell-scripting.
The
.Fl h
switch was added on June 10th,
and a basic man page was written on November 3rd.
.
.Pp
The
.Nm
utility was removed on March 18th 2018 \
in an effort to move away from macOS in favour of
.Ox .
It was restored in January 2019 \
after continued use of macOS became necessary.
Its man page was rewritten to use
.Xr mdoc 7
instead of the original
.Xr man 7
macros.
.
.Pp
.ad l
On August 3rd 2024,
.Nm Ap s
default behaviour was changed to only target files whose full
.Xr basename 3
equals
.Dq .DS_Store ,
rather than targeting anything whose filename ended in that extension.
The former behaviour can be opted-into by passing the
.Fl p
switch.
.
.Pp
On December 30th 2026,
.Nm
was heavily refactored to address several bugs \
related to the consistency of its output;
feedback is no longer affected by failing to set \
modification times of read-only folders, the
.Fl -home
switch may now be used with other
.Pq single-letter
options,
hard-links are now considered when tallying freed-up disk space,
and a symbolic link is now dereferenced when used as
.Nm Ap s
.Ar directory
argument.
The
.Fl g
and
.Fl t
options were also added for skipping Git-tracked files \
and running a suite of built-in unit tests,
respectively.
A backwards-incompatible change was making
.Xr format-bytes 1
a required dependency for formatting byte-counts;
previously,
.Nm
used the utility to format byte-counts only if it was available,
falling back to the less-readable format
.Ql Pq Ar N Sy bytes
in its absence.
.
