.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Nm
utility is intended for use on Apple macOS.
Its usefulness on other systems is limited to \
purging shared network drives and portable media,
which are prone to pollution when written to from macOS.
Moreover,
.Nm
is tailored to the foibles of macOS;
in particular,
it requires a BSD-flavoured version of
.Xr stat 1
to work.
.Pp
Note that
.Nm Ap s
function can also be achieved using
.Xr find 1 ,
albeit without preserving directory modification times:
.Dl Cm find Fl Hs Ar path Fl type Ar f Fl name Ar .DS_Store Fl delete Fl print
.
.Sh BUGS
Compatibility with the GNU implementation of
.Xr stat 1
could be added to facilitate use of
.Nm
on platforms other than macOS.
Similarly,
the script could be rewritten to use features compatible with POSIX
.Xr sh 1 ;
this was made especially pertinent after Apple switched macOS's default shell to
.Xr zsh 1 .
